l services comprising consulting and training. The company was formerly known as 10gen, Inc. and changed its name to MongoDB, Inc. in August 2013. MongoDB, Inc. was incorporated in 2007 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Dev C. Ittycheria | Interim President & CEO and Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $656,743 (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $426K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 41%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $86K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $95K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["MongoDB, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $26.9B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +24% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +7.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -37% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 72% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $500M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -43.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.5%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 22% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 517% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":5.174857375643078},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $25.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Contrasting MongoDB (MDB) & Its Rivals","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/contrasting-mongodb-mdb-its-rivals.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794582916.